---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Invitation from '../components/Invitation.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Alastair Brayne | AI consultant, founder & engineer"
  description="Meet Alastair Brayne: 20+ years in software and CTO roles, an AI startup founder and trained psychotherapist. Fractional and contract AI consultancy through ExFu."
>
  <section class="page-hero about-hero">
    <div class="wrap about-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow red">Hello. I’m Alastair.</p><h1>
          People.<br />Technology.<br />Getting it done.
        </h1><p class="lead">
          I help people turn the possibilities of AI into something useful in their work. ExFu is
          where I bring together experience in business, engineering and working with people.
        </p><a class="text-link" href="/enquire/"
          >Tell me what you’re working on <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </div><figure class="headshot">
        <img
          src="/images/alastair-avatar.webp"
          alt="Pencil sketch portrait of Alastair Brayne"
          width="480"
          height="480"
          fetchpriority="high"
        /><figcaption>Alastair Brayne · Bristol, UK</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="wrap reading-layout section editorial-layout">
    <nav class="contents" aria-label="On this page">
      <p>On this page</p><a href="#approach">How I approach the work</a><a href="#experience"
        >Experience & CVs</a
      ><a href="#tools">Tools out in the open</a><a href="#working">Working together</a>
    </nav><div class="prose editorial-prose">
      <section id="approach">
        <h2>Business judgement. Hands-on engineering. An understanding of people.</h2>
        <p class="lead">Three perspectives shape how I approach the same piece of work.</p>
        <div class="perspective-map" aria-label="Three perspectives brought to the work">
          <div><span>Founder</span><p>Is it worth doing?</p></div>
          <div><span>Engineer</span><p>Can we make it work?</p></div>
          <div><span>Psychotherapist</span><p>How will people use it?</p></div>
        </div>
        <p>
          A useful implementation needs to make sense for the business and for the people using it.
          I bring those questions into the room with the engineering, and stay close to the work as
          we try something concrete.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="experience">
        <h2>Experience behind the approach.</h2>
        <div class="download-links">
          <a
            href="/downloads/alastair-brayne-commercial-cv.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Commercial CV <span>PDF ↗</span></a
          >
          <a
            href="/downloads/alastair-brayne-technical-cv.pdf"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">Technical CV <span>PDF ↗</span></a
          >
        </div>
        <div class="service-rows experience-rows">
          <article>
            <div>
              <h3>Founder</h3><p class="row-answer">Choosing where to put limited time.</p>
            </div><p>
              Five years building an LLM-enabled product startup, alongside consultancy across
              personal agent setup, internal AI work and customer-facing agents. Recent engagements
              include travel and EV sector businesses.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <div>
              <h3>Engineer &amp; technical leader</h3><p class="row-answer">
                Moving between the question and the build.
              </p>
            </div><p>
              More than two decades of full-stack development and technical leadership, including
              CTO work. I can stay hands-on with the implementation as the business decisions
              develop.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <div>
              <h3>People &amp; psychology</h3><p class="row-answer">
                Helping people learn and work with change.
              </p>
            </div><p>
              A degree in AI with psychology, followed by psychotherapy training. That informs how I
              listen, support someone learning an unfamiliar tool, and think about change inside a
              team. ExFu engagements are AI consultancy.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="experience-followup">
          Read the <a href="/fractional-support/#recent-experience">recent project accounts</a>, or <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/albrayne"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">find me on LinkedIn</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section id="tools">
        <h2>Open tools, and a visible way of working.</h2><p>
          I build and share agent tooling through the ExFu marketplace. It includes approaches to
          managing context, planning work and recording the decisions agents make along the way.
        </p><p>
          That is also how this website was developed: human direction, agent implementation, and a
          record of what was chosen and why.
        </p><a
          class="text-link"
          href="https://github.com/exfu/exfu-marketplace"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          >Explore the ExFu marketplace <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
        >
      </section>
      <section id="working">
        <h2>Fractional and contract work.</h2><p>
          I take on fractional and contract engagements, with remote work preferred. I’m based in
          Bristol and can arrange in-person sessions.
        </p><p>
          If you are a founder, a CTO, an internal advocate or a recruiter with a suitable brief,
          I’d be glad to hear what you are trying to move forward. If you are looking for help with
          your own workload, <a href="/personal-support/">personal support</a> may be the right place
          to start.
        </p><p>ExFu is my AI consultancy and tooling brand, operated by WhaleyBear Ltd.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
  <Invitation />
</Layout>
